<title>USA: Solvay unit wins Jeep fuel system pact.</title>
<headline>Solvay unit wins Jeep fuel system pact.</headline>
<dateline>TROY, Mich. 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Solvay Automotive, a unit of the Solvay America Inc division of Belgium-based Solvay SA, said Tuesday it received a contract to provide fuel storage and delivery systems to Chrysler Corp.</p>
<p>Solvay Automotive said it will produce nearly 300,000 plastic-based fuel systems for 1997-model Jeep Wrangler and Cherokee automobiles. The systems include fuel tanks, fuel lines, fuel pumps, fuel-level sensors and roll-over valves.</p>
<p>A spokesman said financial terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Solvay produces a line of molded plastic auto parts.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
